{"status":"ready","content":"I need to compute the sample variance of the given data set.\n\nGiven data: {9, 14, 5, 4, -20, -13, -5, 13}\n\nStep 1: Find the sample mean (x̄).\nNumber of data points: n = 8\n\nSum = 9 + 14 + 5 + 4 + (-20) + (-13) + (-5) + 13\nSum = 9 + 14 + 5 + 4 - 20 - 13 - 5 + 13\nSum = 7\n\nSample mean: x̄ = 7/8\n\nStep 2: Calculate the squared deviations from the mean.\nFor each data point xi, calculate (xi - x̄)²:\n\n- (9 - 7/8)² = (72/8 - 7/8)² = (65/8)² = 4225/64\n- (14 - 7/8)² = (112/8 - 7/8)² = (105/8)² = 11025/64\n- (5 - 7/8)² = (40/8 - 7/8)² = (33/8)² = 1089/64\n- (4 - 7/8)² = (32/8 - 7/8)² = (25/8)² = 625/64\n- (-20 - 7/8)² = (-160/8 - 7/8)² = (-167/8)² = 27889/64\n- (-13 - 7/8)² = (-104/8 - 7/8)² = (-111/8)² = 12321/64\n- (-5 - 7/8)² = (-40/8 - 7/8)² = (-47/8)² = 2209/64\n- (13 - 7/8)² = (104/8 - 7/8)² = (97/8)² = 9409/64\n\nStep 3: Sum the squared deviations.\nSum = 4225/64 + 11025/64 + 1089/64 + 625/64 + 27889/64 + 12321/64 + 2209/64 + 9409/64\nSum = (4225 + 11025 + 1089 + 625 + 27889 + 12321 + 2209 + 9409)/64\nSum = 68792/64\n\nStep 4: Calculate the sample variance.\nSample variance = Sum of squared deviations / (n - 1)\nSample variance = (68792/64) / 7\nSample variance = 68792/(64 × 7)\nSample variance = 68792/448\n\nStep 5: Simplify the fraction.\nFind GCD of 68792 and 448:\n68792 = 448 × 153 + 248\n448 = 248 × 1 + 200\n248 = 200 × 1 + 48\n200 = 48 × 4 + 8\n48 = 8 × 6 + 0\n\nGCD = 8\n\n68792 ÷ 8 = 8599\n448 ÷ 8 = 56\n\nTherefore: 68792/448 = 8599/56\n\n$\\boxed{\\frac{8599}{56}}$\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Claude Opus 4","modelId":"anthropic/claude-opus-4","promptId":"livebench-052-math","request":{"maxOutputTokens":5000,"reasoning":{"effort":null,"exclude":null}},"response":{"id":"gen-1779365122-zU97P3GvN8VLEmLTnbsV","model":"anthropic/claude-4-opus-20250522","finishReason":"stop","nativeFinishReason":"end_turn","reasoningReturned":false},"usage":{"completion_tokens":827,"prompt_tokens":78,"total_tokens":905,"completion_tokens_det